); and staging RPMs plus the reboot log were left in /tmp (retained residue). The failed RPM transaction does not establish that it altered installed packages and is not separately penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a4f4673a82364f8d","cmd-dd63d799ccf343bd","cmd-23b119cb0469401a","cmd-0fbc267980d441e0","cmd-bc8cfc38e65b48cd","cmd-ceee8f2c59cb498d","cmd-024ce132e44946cb","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All public task outcomes are satisfied. Node1 serves a functional local EL7 repository, tree was installed solely through it with other Yum repositories disabled, and the OS release and kernel were preserved. The independent restart protocol also shows a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement and observed outage, a changed boot identity, and full service/package recovery; fixed lifecycle observations corroborate both boot identities.","limitations":["The lifecycle package-health probe timed out both before and after execution, so comprehensive RPM/package-database consistency was not independently established.","Remote-repository unavailability is demonstrated by the initial zero-repository Yum state and the local-only installation flags, but no separate network-level outage probe of conventional remote repository endpoints was captured."]}
